<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  org.nextbsd.bluetoothd.plist

  Boot-time launchd plist for bluetoothd, the NextBSD Bluetooth daemon.

  WHY org.nextbsd.* AND NOT com.apple.*

  Apple's daemon is also called bluetoothd, but its labels and Mach services
  (com.apple.bluetoothd, com.apple.server.bluetooth) are contracts that only
  Apple's closed frameworks look up, and nothing Apple-derived on NextBSD does.
  We write the bluetooth(8) CLI, and the IOBluetooth-shaped Objective-C API
  lives above the Mach line in Gershwin. Both ends are ours, so the label is
  ours, as for wland.

  WHAT BLUETOOTHD DOES

  bluetoothd and bluetooth(8) are the only Bluetooth userland. bluetoothd owns
  controller bring-up and power, discovery, pairing for Classic and LE with one
  store (SCPreferences), the SDP server and client, the HID host and the audio
  roles, and publishes State:/Bluetooth. Bluetooth is on by default; it runs
  as root from boot, so a paired keyboard works at the login window.

  HOW BLUETOOTHD FINDS CONTROLLERS

  NgUbt.kext publishes each controller in the IORegistry as an
  IOBluetoothHostController entry and retires it when the controller goes.
  bluetoothd follows that class with IOServiceAddMatchingNotification,
  first-match and terminated. With no controller it blocks, polls nothing and
  loads no kexts. launchd LaunchEvents (com.apple.iokit.matching) would let
  launchd start bluetoothd only when a controller appears, but libxpc's event
  streams are not there yet, so the job runs at load.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive: starts at boot and respawns on crash. There is no
  launchd service ordering in this port, so bluetoothd opens the SCDynamicStore
  lazily and tolerates configd not being up yet.

  StandardErrorPath / StandardOutPath route the log to
  /var/log/bluetoothd.stderr. Nothing goes to the console.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>org.nextbsd.bluetoothd</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/sbin/bluetoothd</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>MachServices</key>
    <dict>
        <key>org.nextbsd.bluetooth</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/bluetoothd.stderr</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/bluetoothd.stderr</string>
</dict>
</plist>
